SWEET Bluetooth: patch 0218 (T-86c9/T-60ed, Opus-reviewed, ran in bt-up7p) carried unchanged in code onto the 0219-0226 lineage as 0228 (ticket T-0d4e, W-BTSCAN): the 0218 hunks re-based against the tree after 0226 (context only; 2 hunks needed fuzz 1, no line of code changed), so the download runs after the sweetbtleprobe=4 sweep and its final power-cycle and bluetoothd meets the patched controller. Original description follows.

SWEET Bluetooth: stock BCM.hcd download into the controller RAM before bluetoothd starts (patch 0218, ticket T-86c9, W-BTUP; boot-arg sweetbtpatchram=1, default off, default behaviour unchanged; sub-knob sweetbtpatchrambaud=1 adds the HAL's 4 Mbaud step, default 115200). bt-up5/bt-up6 [obs 20261104T054627Z-bt-up5, 20261107T030249Z-bt-up6]: bluetoothd lives 23-24 s on the unpatched BCM4389 ROM (0x1001 rev word 0x2000 = build 0, HCI 5.1) while every stock capture shows rev 0x20cb = build 203, HCI 5.2 after the HAL's download (docs/research/BT-rom-vs-patched.md s.4-6; the 3039 records of the vendor BCM.hcd are byte-identical to the golden vendor snoop). After the baud probe settled (and after the 0216/0217 probes, if on), the backend sends the HAL sequence: HCI Reset, 0xfc79 (expect chip id 0xaa, build 0), [0xfc18 4 000 000 and the host UART follows], 0xfc2e download mode + 50 ms, the 3038 x 0xfc4c Write RAM records without Command Complete (RTS/CTS paced, only the first and last record enter the HCI trace so the 3000-transfer cap is left to bluetoothd), 0xfc4e Launch RAM with a Command Complete, [host back to 115200], 250 ms, Reset, 0xfc79 (expect build 203), 0x1001 (expect rev 0x20cb), 0xfc01 Write BD_ADDR with the synthetic 02:00:00:00:00:01 D-3 address and a 0x1009 read-back; no 0xfc27 LPM (host-wake irq not wired), logged as a deviation. Rows: `BT PROBE: patchram ...`, the summary `BT PROBE: patchram build=<n> hci_rev=0x<r> records=3039 sha256=<h>`; every missing Command Complete or status != 0 is a `BT GAP:` and stops the sequence, after which the controller is power-cycled back to the ROM for bluetoothd. The firmware is NOT in git: bsd/dev/sweet_bt_hcd.c is an empty slot (len 0 = the knob refuses with a `BT GAP:` and sends nothing); tools/bcm-hcd-stack generates a local-only patch that fills the slot from a gitignored BCM.hcd and prints its sha256. Before any byte is sent the image is scanned: only 0xfc4c writes and one final 0xfc4e launch of 4 bytes, lengths adding up to the file size (anything else, e.g. a flash/NVRAM opcode, is refused). sbu_tx is split into the traced sbu_tx and the untraced sbu_tx_raw. Volatile controller RAM only, cleared by REG_ON low [guess: no BCM4389 source says the patch does not persist]. Applies after 0189, 0213, 0215, 0216 and 0217. Review T-60ed (Opus round 1) fixes: the first/last stream record logs a header-only `BT HCI: tx ... (payload not logged)` row (no firmware bytes in logs/proofs); stream rx bytes or line errors, a launch that does not answer build 203 / rev 0x20cb, and a BD_ADDR read-back mismatch each stop the sequence (EIO -> power-cycle back to the ROM); the start row prints `stock=yes|no` against the stock sha256 and a GAP when no; attach-side recovery lives in sbu_patchram_attach() (host-tested); the knob logs a GAP also when attach returns before the download. Not run on hardware yet.

